From: u9e12eec50c435b60 at groups.google.com (Arthur Georges)
Date: Wed, 20 Nov 2019 01:38:05 +0000
Subject: Re: [dartR] Population names - how to completely change
Message-ID: <pNUo7rbDmhU.em2AcQNTBwAJ@dartr.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <pNUo7rbDmhU.Jg0D-cRSBwAJ@dartr.groups.google.com>
References: <pNUo7rbDmhU.Jg0D-cRSBwAJ@dartr.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/dartr/c/pNUo7rbDmhU/m/em2AcQNTBwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Olly,

The solution is to have your new finer scale sampling sites as a variable in your individual metrics (added when you read the data in), then use gl.reassign.pop() to assign that metric to the pop slot.

A

